    hints: ['Start count at 0 and visit each input value.', 'Compare the current value with limit using <.', 'Increase count only for a match, but always advance the position.'],
    explanation: 'The comparison makes a yes/no decision for each item. A matching item contributes exactly 1 to the count. Keeping position advancement outside the condition ensures both matching and nonmatching values are visited once.',
    solution: 'count = 0\nposition = 0\nwhile position < len(values):\n    if values[position] < limit:\n        count = count + 1\n    position = position + 1\nresult = count\n',
